WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.680 --> 00:00:03.720
They say our people
were born on the water.

00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:08.580
The very first enslaved
Africans were brought

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.320
here over 400 years ago.

00:00:10.320 --> 00:00:12.720
Since then, no part
of America's story

00:00:12.720 --> 00:00:15.000
has been untouched by
the legacy of slavery.

00:00:16.320 --> 00:00:18.360
This is The 1619 Project.

00:00:18.360 --> 00:00:19.620
The New York Times.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:21.000
1619 project.

00:00:21.000 --> 00:00:22.680
It is the legacy of slavery.

00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:25.260
My father, he always flew&nbsp;
a flag in our front yard.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.320
One thing about
dad, he was patriotic.

00:00:28.320 --> 00:00:30.420
He was a part of
the United States Army.

00:00:30.420 --> 00:00:31.440
They served their country.

00:00:31.440 --> 00:00:34.200
But hey, you served country
don't mean your country

00:00:34.200 --> 00:00:34.740
going to serve you.

00:00:34.740 --> 00:00:38.940
The truth is Black Americans

00:00:38.940 --> 00:00:42.600
have always been foundational
to the idea of American freedom.

00:00:42.600 --> 00:00:45.180
Democracy is a fight.

00:00:45.180 --> 00:00:47.804
It will always be a fight.

00:00:47.804 --> 00:00:47.820
Stand and fight.

00:00:47.820 --> 00:00:52.140
You are calling
for reparations.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.300
What is the total
that would be owed?

00:00:54.300 --> 00:00:55.200
$14 trillion.

00:00:55.200 --> 00:00:56.880
- That's a big number.
- Yeah.

00:00:56.880 --> 00:00:57.660
Big debt, though.

00:00:57.660 --> 00:00:58.740
It is a big debt.

00:00:58.740 --> 00:00:59.880
We are still fighting.

00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:01.860
As long as there's life,
we're going to have hope.

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:06.240
When I hear Funk,
I hear freedom.

00:01:06.240 --> 00:01:09.420
There are centuries
in that music.

00:01:09.420 --> 00:01:12.060
Centuries in that spirit.

00:01:14.580 --> 00:01:16.980
The 1619 Project,
it's not a history.

00:01:16.980 --> 00:01:20.400
It really is talking
about America today.

00:01:21.360 --> 00:01:24.540
Black Americans
contributions are undeniable.

00:01:25.380 --> 00:01:29.220
No people had a greater claim
to the American flag than we do.

